Package: RepliAPA
Title: Replicate-Aware Inference for Alternative Polyadenylation
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Wei", family = "Xu",
    email = "xw222300@163.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Transparent guide- and replicate-aware inference for changes in
    alternative polyadenylation composition. The package aggregates cell-level
    polyadenylation counts to biological sample units, estimates equal-guide
    all-site composition effects, performs exhaustive guide-identity permutation
    tests while preserving replicate blocks, calibrates inference with
    guide-unit non-targeting contrasts, and reports gene-expression effects,
    guide heterogeneity, cross-context robustness, post-freeze orthogonal
    direction support, strong-baseline interoperability, pre-fit input
    adequacy, checksum-protected result bundles, measured compute provenance
    and abstention explicitly. A fingerprinted v1-candidate contract freezes
    exported signatures, S3 result components, result-table schemas, and
    compatibility policy for auditable downstream integrations.
